<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para><term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip"> Functions</term> \(R\) and \(D\) give the height, in feet, of a toy rocket and a drone, \(t\) seconds after they are released. Here are the graphs of \(R\) (for the rocket) and \(D\) (for the drone).</para>
<media><image alt="Two functions graphed on a cooridnate plane." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6953fee5f8d02223583c335e6d1949b8e372de5f"/></media><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Which of the inequalities is true: \(R(2)&gt;D(2)\) or \(D(2)&gt; R(2)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(R(2)&gt;D(2)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What was the height of the drone when the toy rocket hit the ground?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>20 feet</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>For what value of \(t\) is \(R(t)=D(t)\) true?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>About \(t=4.5\). </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What does this tell you about the drone and the toy rocket?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>After 4.5 seconds, the toy rocket and the drone are at the same height.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
